 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# HR Employee Attrition Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** identify employee segments with elevated attrition and quantify relationships between workforce factors and turnover.\n",
    "\n",
    "> Dataset note: this project uses synthetic HR data generated for analytical practice."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(99)\n",
    "n = 5000\n",
    "departments = ['Engineering', 'Sales', 'HR', 'Marketing', 'Finance', 'Operations']\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'EmployeeID': [f'EMP{i:04d}' for i in range(1, n + 1)],\n",
    "    'Age': rng.integers(22, 60, n),\n",
    "    'Department': rng.choice(departments, n),\n",
    "    'MonthlyIncome': np.round(rng.uniform(3000, 20000, n), 2),\n",
    "    'YearsAtCompany': rng.integers(0, 20, n),\n",
    "    'JobSatisfaction': rng.integers(1, 5, n),\n",
    "    'WorkLifeBalance': rng.integers(1, 5, n),\n",
    "    'OverTime': rng.integers(0, 2, n),\n",
    "    'YearsSinceLastPromotion': rng.integers(0, 10, n),\n",
    "    'DistanceFromHome': rng.integers(1, 50, n),\n",
    "})\n",
    "score = (-0.30 * df.JobSatisfaction - 0.20 * df.WorkLifeBalance + 0.40 * df.OverTime - 0.15 * np.log1p(df.YearsAtCompany) + 0.05 * df.YearsSinceLastPromotion + 0.15 * df.DistanceFromHome / 50 + rng.normal(0, .3, n))\n",
    "prob = 1 / (1 + np.exp(-score))\n",
    "df['Attrition'] = (rng.random(n) < prob).astype(int)\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## KPI Summary"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summary = pd.Series({\n",
    "Employees": len(df),\n",
    "Attrition Rate (%)": round(df.Attrition.mean() * 100, 2),\n",
    "Average Monthly Income": round(df.MonthlyIncome.mean(), 2),\n",
    "Average Tenure (years)": round(df.YearsAtCompany.mean(), 2),\n",
    "Overtime Share (%)": round(df.OverTime.mean() * 100, 2),\n",
    "})\n",
    "summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Attrition by Department"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "department_attrition = (df.groupby('Department').Attrition.agg(['count', 'sum', 'mean']).rename(columns={'count': 'Employees', 'sum': 'Attrited', 'mean': 'AttritionRate'}))\n",
    "department_attrition['AttritionRate'] = (department_attrition['AttritionRate'] * 100).round(2)\n",
    "department_attrition.sort_values('AttritionRate', ascending=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Workforce Drivers"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "numeric = df.select_dtypes('number')\n",
    "correlations = numeric.corr()['Attrition'].drop('Attrition').sort_values(key=abs, ascending=False)\n",
    "correlations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "correlations.sort_values().plot.barh(ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Correlation with Employee Attrition')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Pearson correlation')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Interpretation\n", "\n", "Correlation does not establish causation. The strongest relationships should be treated as signals for further HR investigation, not proof that a single factor causes employees to leave."]
  }
 ],
